  "notes": "USAGE:\n{薄|うす}れる is an intransitive ichidan verb. The transitive counterpart is {薄|うす}める (to dilute, to thin). Both senses describe a gradual process of becoming less intense.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記憶|きおく}が{薄|うす}れる (memories fade)\n- {意識|いしき}が{薄|うす}れる (consciousness fades / awareness diminishes)\n- {存在感|そんざいかん}が{薄|うす}れる (presence diminishes)\n- {影響力|えいきょうりょく}が{薄|うす}れる (influence wanes)\n- {色|いろ}が{薄|うす}れる (color fades)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {消|き}える: to disappear (complete, not gradual)\n- {衰|おとろ}える: to decline, to weaken (for strength, power, vitality)\n- {褪|あ}せる: to fade, to discolor (mainly for colors and dyes)",
